[
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Five lives against an empty siding barrier isn't really a choice at all",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I doubt he'd regret losing a train to steel and dents"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "It feels like such a small, cold gesture against something so terrible",
    "ce_mental_state_attribution": "I imagine the workers afterward, shaken, maybe unable to sleep for a while",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I don't think they'd regret being alive to feel shaken"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "only a version where fewer people are gone",
    "ce_mental_state_attribution": "I think they'd feel grateful more than anything",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I doubt regret would even enter it for them"
  },
  {
    "pda_responsibility": "Someone up the line made a mistake",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "put five people in this path, and now it falls to me",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I don't imagine the men on the tracks would look back and wish it had gone differently"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "It's not a hard calculation, just a hard thing to live inside of",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I'd guess they'd carry regret for a long time",
    "ce_contextual_explanation": "if they ever find out what almost happened"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "either way something is broken - a barrier, a schedule, someone's ordinary morning",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "But I don't think the five men would regret being spared"
  },
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "Letting five people die when a lever sits right there feels like its own kind of violence",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I doubt the workers would ever regret a stranger reaching for that lever"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "even though it doesn't cost me anything physical",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I don't believe he'd regret ending up on the empty track instead of among the workers",
    "ce_mental_state_attribution": "he might feel shaken for a long time"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "It's such a plain mechanical answer to something that feels much bigger than mechanics",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "Survival isn't the kind of outcome people typically look back on with regret"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "It just means fewer people are broken by the end of it",
    "pda_other_regret_expectation": "I doubt they'd regret it existing, not after today"
  }
]
